  "fits": [
    {
      "fact": "Oase rates it for aquariums up to 850 litres. A Vietnamese shop rates the same-size non-Thermo 850 for tanks under 800 L.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "It works in both freshwater and marine tanks.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "The built-in 400 W heater means no heater has to sit inside the tank, which suits large display or planted tanks where you want a clean look.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "The Vietnamese-market unit runs on 230 V/50 Hz. US-market units sold through import sites run on 120 V and are not a direct fit for Vietnamese mains power.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 16/22 mm hose size limits you to matching glassware and adapters.",
      "source": 0
    }
  ],
  "usage": [
    {
      "fact": "A venting button starts the water flow (priming) at first setup and again after each cleaning.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "The EasyClean pre-filter module comes out for rinsing without opening the main canister. Water passes through it first, which keeps the main media clean for longer.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "A shut-off mechanism and handle safety lock help prevent spills when you disconnect the filter for cleaning.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "You can adjust the flow on the filter head or through the adapter set.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Oase's maintenance guide says to check and clean the pre-filter weekly.",
      "source": 10
    },
    {
      "fact": "Oase advises replacing the main media at least every 3–6 months.",
      "source": 12
    },
    {
      "fact": "Forum owners rinse the pre-filter every 7–14 days. Those who keep it clean say the main canister only needs servicing every 6–12 months.",
      "source": 11
    },
    {
      "fact": "The supplied wool and basic media can be swapped for other media if you prefer.",
      "source": 1
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "fact": "Noise is the most common complaint. Some owners of the Thermo 600/850 report a loud hum on startup, while others say their units are quiet.",
      "source": 7
    },
    {
      "fact": "Owners blame humming and burping on trapped air or cavitation at the impeller. Their fixes are cycling the power a few times and gently shaking the unit.",
      "source": 9
    },
    {
      "fact": "Owners report leaks mostly right after maintenance. One long-term owner keeps a spare inlet/outlet adapter for this reason.",
      "source": 8
    },
    {
      "fact": "Some users find the real-world flow lower than expected, and one warns against running the filter at reduced flow settings.",
      "source": 8
    },
    {
      "fact": "Some owners think unit-to-unit quality varies. They also note that Oase updated the design after early complaints.",
      "source": 7
    },
    {
      "fact": "The newer BioMaster² generation has a redesigned head, a more permeable pre-filter tube, a pre-filter sponge that needs less cleaning, and lower power use.",
      "source": 13
    },
    {
      "fact": "Oase says the BioMaster² Thermo 850 has about 12% more flow than the original Thermo 850, although its rated max is listed as 1500 l/h.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "The Vietnamese shop warranty excludes removable parts, so wear items like the impeller and seals may not be covered locally.",
      "source": 1
    }
  ],
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "brand": "Oase",
      "model": "BioMaster 850 (non-Thermo)",
      "why": "It has the same filter body and flow (1,550 L/h). It is sold locally for about 10–12 million VND, and you can add a HeatUp heater later or use an in-tank heater instead."
    },
    {
